---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Support - Manuel Gil - Open Source Maintainer"
  description="If the tools I've published are useful to you, you can help offset the cost of carrying them."
  keywords="support, sponsor, open source, maintainer"
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 pt-20">
    <section class="flex items-center justify-center py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h1
          class="mb-4 bg-linear-to-r from-primary to-accent bg-clip-text text-6xl font-bold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-transparent"
        >
          Support
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-8 text-xl text-zinc-400">
          If these tools are useful to you and you want them to keep existing, you can help.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">What Support Enables</h2>
        <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-zinc-400">
          I carry these projects alone, without corporate backing. The time I spend on
          bug fixes, dependency updates, and compatibility work is unpaid.
          Sponsorship helps offset that time so the tools can keep existing.
        </p>
        <ul class="mb-6 space-y-2 text-zinc-400">
          <li class="flex items-center">
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            Keeping existing tools compatible where possible
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center">
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            Offsetting the personal time spent on bug fixes and dependency updates
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center">
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            Allowing this work to continue without turning it into a product
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">What Support Does Not Buy</h2>
        <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-zinc-400">
          Sponsorship doesn't buy features, access, or priority. It doesn't create an obligation
          or a service relationship. It's a way to enable continuity for tools that are freely
          available to everyone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto mb-16 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">How to Support</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-zinc-400">
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/sponsors/ManuelGil"
              class="text-primary transition-colors hover:text-primary-dark"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              GitHub Sponsors →
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/ManuelGil"
              class="text-primary transition-colors hover:text-primary-dark"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Buy me a coffee →
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto mb-32 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold">People Who Help</h2>
        <ul class="mb-6 space-y-2 text-zinc-400">
          <li>
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/sebasttti"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-primary">Juan Sebastian Joya R.</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="mr-2 text-primary">▹</span>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/djmai"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-primary">Miguel Martinez</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
